invariant: INV-5
file: webpki_name.c
catches: webpki_name_test
reason: dropping the GeneralName tag check lets read_entry take the
  first byte of a high-tag-number header (9f 1f ...) as the whole tag
  and the next byte as the length, so the walk frames later entries at
  the wrong offsets and matches a dNSName hidden inside another entry's
  content. Universal tags such as 04 and 00 are then skipped as entries.
  bin/webpki_name_test's tag rows object.

--- old
    if (!is_general_name_tag(tag)) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    (void)is_general_name_tag;
